      <div class="jt-pane" id="pane-sales">
        <div>
          <h3>A pipeline that fits how you sell.</h3>
          <p>Drag deals across the board, with stages you name. Every enquiry from wa.me links,
          click-to-WhatsApp ads or your website button lands on the board with its history
          beside it — assigned by queue, stage or language.</p>
          <div class="metric-cards">
            <div class="metric-card"><b>Stages</b><span>you define</span></div>
            <div class="metric-card"><b>Notes</b><span>kept internal</span></div>
            <div class="metric-card"><b>CSV</b><span>import with dedupe</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="btn-row"><a class="btn" href="/features/sales-pipelines">Explore pipelines &rarr;</a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="shot"><img src="/docs/screenshots/pipelines-view.png" alt="Sales pipeline" width="780" height="546" loading="lazy" /></div>
      </div>

      <div class="jt-pane" id="pane-support">
        <div>
          <h3>The 24-hour window, handled.</h3>
          <p>A live countdown on every open chat; the composer switches to approved templates
          automatically when the service window closes; unread and mention filters keep
          nothing waiting quietly; out-of-hours auto-replies buy time until morning.</p>
          <div class="metric-cards">
            <div class="metric-card"><b>Live</b><span>window timer</span></div>
            <div class="metric-card"><b>Auto</b><span>template fallback</span></div>
            <div class="metric-card"><b>1 step</b><span>agent takeover</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="btn-row"><a class="btn" href="/features/shared-inbox">Explore the inbox &rarr;</a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="shot"><img src="/docs/screenshots/inbox-conversation.png" alt="Shared inbox conversation" width="780" height="546" loading="lazy" /></div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section sec-white">
  <div class="wrap orbit-wrap">
    <div class="shot" style="order:0"><img src="/docs/screenshots/agents-view.png" alt="AI drafts playground" width="720" height="506" loading="lazy" /></div>
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Assisted, not autonomous</p>
      <h2>AI drafts, grounded in your own documents.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Upload your product docs and WebPing drafts replies from them — pricing,
      policies, the things your team actually types. A human always reviews and hits
      send; automation can be muted per chat by keyword or sentiment.</p>
      <ul class="pi-list">
        <li><span class="tick"></span><span><b>Grounded</b> in uploaded docs, not hallucinated features.</span></li>
        <li><span class="tick"></span><span><b>Human-guided</b> — nothing sends from drafts without a person approving it.</span></li>
        <li><span class="tick"></span><span><b>Interruptible</b> — agents take over any chat in one step.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <div class="btn-row"><a class="btn-ghost" href="/features/ai-assistant">About AI drafts &rarr;</a></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section sec-mint">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker">For developers</p>
      <h2>Plugs into what you already run.</h2>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-top:12px">A small, honest API surface: create contacts, trigger
      broadcasts, read conversations. Replace nothing — extend what you have.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="int-grid">
      <div class="int-card"><span class="itag">REST API</span><h3>Every object, scoped keys</h3><p>Contacts, conversations, broadcasts and templates through versioned endpoints with scoped API keys.</p></div>
      <div class="int-card"><span class="itag">Webhooks</span><h3>Signed events</h3><p>Message received, chat assigned, broadcast done — outgoing events signed with HMAC-SHA256.</p></div>
      <div class="int-card"><span class="itag">Templates</span><h3>Approved message templates</h3><p>Sync with Meta's library, submit for approval, then use them in broadcasts and automations.</p></div>
      <div class="int-card"><span class="itag">Contacts</span><h3>CSV import &amp; fields</h3><p>Column mapping, dedupe on phone number, tags and custom fields created in chat.</p></div>
      <div class="int-card"><span class="itag">Quick replies</span><h3>Speed in the composer</h3><p>Team-wide saved replies with variables, one keystroke away while a customer waits.</p></div>
      <div class="int-card"><span class="itag">No account</span><h3>Free tools</h3><p>wa.me link generator and a chat button for any website — use them before you sign up.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="codebox" style="margin-top:34px"><pre><span class="cm"># Send a message through WebPing</span>
curl -X POST "https://webping.webpeaker.com/api/v1/messages" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $WEBPING_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"phone":"919867543210","template":"order_shipped","lang":"en","variables":["#1042","Aug 7"]}'</pre></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section sec-deep">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.05fr .95fr;gap:44px;align-items:end">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Yours, end to end</p>
        <h2>Built to hold every conversation.</h2>
      </div>
      <p style="color:var(--sub);font-size:1.05rem;margin:0">Shared inbox and an honest API aren't
      add-ons — they're the point. Prices don't hide Meta's charges, data doesn't leave your
      server, and the refund isn't ornamental.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-row">
      <div class="stat"><b>1</b><span>number for the whole team</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>24 h</b><span>window, with a live timer</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>2</b><span>plans — no maze</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>0</b><span>middlemen between you and your data</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="trust-card">
      <div class="seals">
        <span class="seal" style="background:var(--green)">WAPI</span>
        <span class="seal" style="background:#38bdf8">TLS</span>
        <span class="seal" style="background:#8b5cf6">RSA</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Security and privacy, on your own stack.</h3>
        <p>TLS 1.3 in transit, encrypted at rest, scoped API keys, signed webhooks, audit trail on permissions.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="go" href="/security">Read the security notes &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

